# Template Tags 🏷️

Tags provide logic in templates using `{% tag %}`.

## If/Else Statements

```html
{% if user.is_authenticated %}
    <p>Welcome back, {{ user.username }}!</p>
    <a href="{% url 'logout' %}">Logout</a>
{% elif user.is_guest %}
    <p>Welcome, Guest! Consider signing up.</p>
{% else %}
    <p>Please <a href="{% url 'login' %}">log in</a></p>
{% endif %}

<!-- Comparison operators -->
{% if score >= 90 %}
    <span class="grade-a">Excellent!</span>
{% elif score >= 70 %}
    <span class="grade-b">Good job!</span>
{% elif score >= 50 %}
    <span class="grade-c">Passed</span>
{% else %}
    <span class="grade-f">Try again</span>
{% endif %}

<!-- Boolean operators -->
{% if user.is_authenticated and user.is_verified %}
    <p>Full access granted</p>
{% endif %}

{% if not user.is_banned %}
    <button>Post Comment</button>
{% endif %}
```

## Checking Membership

```html
{% if 'admin' in user.roles %}
    <a href="/admin/">Admin Panel</a>
{% endif %}

{% if item in shopping_cart %}
    <button>Remove from Cart</button>
{% else %}
    <button>Add to Cart</button>
{% endif %}
```
